1.1.text:
Part Five
Form and Mechanism of Service for Handling Victims of Violence Article 9 (1) Forms of handling services for victims of violence organized by P2TP2A include:
a. medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service, especially Visum et Repertum and Visum et Repertum Psichiatricum, for the purpose of evidence in the judicial process, starting from the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court levels;
c. legal aid services to assist victims of violence in undergoing the judicial process;
d. spiritual services for moral strengthening according to the religion and beliefs adhered to;
e. first psychosocial assistance to victims is carried out to identify the occurrence of violence and trauma experienced by victims; f. accompaniment of victims of violence carried out by competent persons or institutions that have expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the strengthening and recovery of victims of violence and have cooperated with P2TP2T or other names;
g. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and provision of economic access so that victims can be economically independent; and
h. services to return and or remain in educational institutions for child victims of violence.
(2) The implementation of handling services for women and children victims of violence is carried out: quickly, safely and comfortably, with a sense of empathy, non-discrimination, easily accessible, free of charge and guaranteed confidentiality.
(3) The mechanism and procedures for implementing handling services technically for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) are organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) and further regulated by Regent Regulation.

REGENT OF BLITAR
REGIONAL REGULATION OF BLITAR REGENCY
NUMBER 11 OF 2013
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF BLITAR,

a. that women and children are beings created by Almighty God who have noble rights and dignity in accordance with their nature as human beings;
b. that there are still many women and children who do not fully receive their basic rights, especially women and children who are victims of violence;
c. that all forms of acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of Human Rights, so that women and children who are victims of violence need to receive protection;
d. that the protection of women and children, especially victims of violence, is one of the obligations that must be carried out by the Regional Government as one of the efforts to realize community welfare;
e. that to realize protection for women and children who are victims of violence in an integrated and sustainable manner, institutional support and legislation are needed that can guarantee its implementation in a coordinated and directed manner;

Considering: :
f. that based on considerations a, b, c, d, and e, it is necessary to immediately establish a Regional Regulation of Blitar Regency concerning the Protection of Women and Children

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution; 2. Law Number 12 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of East Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 41), as amended by Law Number 2 of 1965 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1965 Number 19, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3851);
